 "source_sha256": "043f1f5bda149e106b9fc1fb50ea1596f0dc983f72d8a6e89e9d897c10a0ce68",
 "purpose": "The clock window process: a real analogue clock in its own tkinter window next to the terminal, driven by JSON lines on stdin and answering on stdout.",
 "details": "Run as `python -m leeravontuur.venster.klokvenster` by terminal/venster.py (Klokvenster). It never runs inside the curses process, so tkinter and curses cannot disturb each other and a window problem cannot freeze the program. Protocol: stdin takes {doe: toon|verberg|stop, ...}, stdout sends {klaar} or {fout} at start, {toets}, {klik: [dx, dy]} (where the minute hand should point), {plek: [x, y, w, h]} (the user moved the window) and {dicht}. The window stays on top while a clock is shown, does not take the keyboard from the terminal (WS_EX_NOACTIVATE on Windows, a utility window on Linux), is placed next to the terminal or top right, at most a quarter of the screen wide, and remembers a position the user chose (LEERAVONTUUR_KLOKPLEK). The shapes come from klokbeeld.vormen. The window-geometry helpers (maat_voor, kies_plek, monitor_van, lees_geometrie) are pure functions that tests call directly.",
 "module_docstring": "Het klokvenster: een echte wijzerklok in een eigen venster (tkinter), naast de terminal.",
